    "Romantic songs, show tunes, and movie songs serve different listening moods; appealing vocals alone do not make them substitutes for the Christmas music I chose.",
    "Around The Campfire gives me too little evidence of a connection, and Wilson Phillips: Greatest Hits feels less connected to my holiday and vocal-group listening to prompt a choice."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to assume that enjoying vocal music means I also want romantic, theatrical, and movie-song albums.",
    "A broadly polished vocal sound seems to count too much when the songs' theme and the vocal-group feel matter more to my choice today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several of my past choices were explicitly Christmas albums, including a repeated title, so that theme deserves more weight than a loose similarity in singing style.",
    "My latest interaction suggests continued interest in vocal-group music, but my older holiday purchases were clustered in November; they do not establish that I want Christmas music on every visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in Christmas music and appealing vocals, but stretched that into other song styles that give me little reason to listen today."
}
